// reviews pack -- client-agnostic storefront reviews (memql#4139, promoted
// into the default build by epic memql#5532).
//
// Net-new PACK, not core. dsl/todos, dsl/calendar, dsl/campaigns stay
// untouched and this domain cannot shadow them.
//
// Config (criteria copy, public display toggle) is DATA on reviewSettings,
// not .memql source -- a client hides/shows without a rebuild. On-storefront
// only; no GBP / marketplace ingest.
//
// EVERY ROW CARRIES THE STORE IT WAS WRITTEN AGAINST (design D9, issue
// memql#5552). The Shopify mirror is safe under preview because it is scoped
// by storeId: an order placed against the development store never appears in
// a read scoped to the live one. These rows are MemQL-origin and had no such
// scope, so a review submitted while previewing a storefront would be a real
// row in the one database, visible to the shoppers of the live store. The
// field is stamped SERVER-SIDE from the binding the write arrived through
// and is refused as a form field, which is the half of D9 that cannot be
// expressed in a schema.
//
// STOREFRONT PACK CONVENTION: concepts, mutations, tools, builtins and
// queries -- NO automations and NO logic. A client's process attaches from
// its own repository with `use reviews.concepts.{ review }` and
// `@trigger(concept="v1:reviews:review")`. reviewspack and the wholesale
// pack keep this; deploypack and referencepack ship both, so it is a choice
// the storefront packs made rather than a rule of the platform.

@version("1.2.0")
@description("A storefront product review. Merchandising stays on the store; this row is the review body plus optional image attachment ids. Images export as files (bytes), not URLs. Whether it is shown is NOT a field: it is derived from the append-only reviewDecision log against the revision the row holds now.")
@displayCard(primary="title", secondary="body", tertiary="productHandle")
@rowAuthz(owner="ownerUserId", clusterOwner, account="accountId")
concept review {
  ownerUserId         string!   @description("v1:identity:user.id of the MERCHANT this review belongs to -- the owner of the deployable it was submitted through, NOT its author. A shopper is nobody to MemQL: they have no user row, no session and no actor, so a review's author is authorName and authorEmail below and nothing else (epic memql#5532, issue memql#5550). This is the single most important sentence in the pack. On the shopper path it is stamped from actor.userId under the site owner's BORROWED authority -- the campaigns precedent, where the drain worker runs everything owned under a userId copied off a row the starting caller had already read. On the authenticated path it is the calling user, which is what an operator or an importing job writes as.")
  storeId             string!   @description("The v1:shopify:store this review was written against (design D9). Stamped server-side from the binding the write arrived through -- the serving binding, or the PREVIEW binding when the submission was made while exercising a candidate version -- and never accepted from a form: component/memql/shopper_surface.go refuses a declared field with this name, and the bff stamps it after the declared fields so a form-supplied copy cannot win. Every storefront read filters on it, which is what keeps a review written under preview out of the live storefront.")
  siteId              string    @description("The v1:platform:site this review was submitted through. Provenance rather than scope: storeId above is what reads filter on, because two deployables may serve one store. Empty on a review written through the authenticated path, which arrived through no site at all.")
  productHandle       string!   @description("Storefront product handle this review is about.")
  productId           string    @description("Optional Shopify product GID when the thin index is present.")
  title               string    @description("Optional short title.")
  body                string!   @description("Review text.")
  rating              int       @description("Optional 1-5 star rating. Sentiment analysis is not a field and must not be added.")
  authorName          string    @description("What the shopper called themselves. DATA, never an identity: nothing authenticates it and no read is scoped by it. A storefront renders it beside the review exactly as submitted.")
  authorEmail         string    @description("The shopper's email as they typed it. DATA, never an identity, and never verified -- it exists so a merchant can reply, and it is why the public read must not project it. A pack that later wants a verified buyer uses the Customer Account API principal recorded as the answer to Q2's second half, not this field.")
  imageAttachmentIds  []string  @description("v1:common:attachment ids for review images. Export resolves these to bytes, never to a remote URL as the payload.")
  createdAtClient     datetime  @description("Client-supplied authored-at watermark. The row intrinsic createdAt remains the version clock.")
  accountId           string    @description("The v1:accounts:account organization the store's deployable belongs to, copied from the site the review arrived through. The account grant: the people of that organization read and moderate the store's reviews without owning them. Empty on a row written before organizations reached reviews, which stays its owner's and the operators'.")
  requestId           string    @description("The v1:reviews:reviewRequest this review was written through -- the buyer's link. Empty on the authenticated path (an operator or an import), which no link vouches for.")
  verifiedBuyer       bool      @description("True only when the review was written through a buyer's link minted from a paid order line. Stamped server-side, never accepted from a form. A storefront shows 'Verified Buyer' for exactly this.")
  revision            int       @description("1 for the first submission through a link, one more for each edit through the same link while it is open. Each edit is a new VERSION of this row; a decision covers the revision it was made on and no other. Absent on older rows, which read as 1.")
  erasedAt            datetime  @description("When the writer's data was erased on request: name, email, title and body blanked in every saved version. An erased review is never shown again.")
}

@version("1.1.0")
@description("Append-only moderation decision for a review. A new row is a new decision; there is no in-place update and no undo-by-overwrite. decidedBy is a Client principal -- a Provider operator cannot author one. Criterion is a closed enum: no other, no sentiment.")
@displayCard(primary="criterion", secondary="reviewId", tertiary="decidedBy")
@rowAuthz(owner="decidedBy", clusterOwner)
concept moderationAction {
  reviewId    string!  @description("v1:reviews:review.id this decision applies to.")
  storeId     string!  @description("The store the moderated review belongs to (design D9), copied from that review by the Go capability rather than supplied. A decision is scoped to the same store its subject is, or a read scoped to one store would show a review the other store's merchant had already hidden.")
  criterion   enum("spam", "profanity", "harassment", "off_topic", "illegal", "copyright")!  @description("Closed moderation criterion. There is no other and no free-text reason. Sentiment is not a criterion.")
  decidedBy   string!  @description("v1:identity:user.id of the Client principal that authored this action. Provider operators are refused on the write path.")
  principalKind enum("client")!  @description("The only expressible principal kind is client. provider is inexpressible -- the enum does not contain it.")
  note        string   @description("Optional client-visible note. Not a criterion and not a sentiment score.")
}

@version("1.0.0")
@description("One moderation decision on one review, append-only: a new row is a new decision, there is no update and no undo-by-overwrite. A review's state (waiting, published, declined, removed, erased) is DERIVED from these rows against the revision the review holds now. decidedBy is a person on the store's side; the cluster's operators are refused on the write path.")
@displayCard(primary="action", secondary="reviewId", tertiary="decidedBy")
@rowAuthz(owner="ownerUserId", clusterOwner, account="accountId")
concept reviewDecision {
  ownerUserId  string!  @description("v1:identity:user.id of the MERCHANT the review belongs to, copied off the review -- not the person who decided (that is decidedBy). OWNED BY THE MERCHANT ON PURPOSE: the public read runs under the site owner's borrowed authority, and a decision that only its author could read would hide or publish nothing (the legacy moderationAction, owned by decidedBy, had exactly that flaw).")
  reviewId   string!  @description("v1:reviews:review.id this decision is about.")
  storeId    string!  @description("The store the review belongs to (design D9), read off the review rather than supplied.")
  accountId  string   @description("The review's organization, copied off the review, so the store's people read the log their colleagues wrote.")
  action     enum("publish", "decline", "askToFix", "escalate", "remove", "erase")!  @description("publish shows the review and closes its link; decline withholds it for a listed reason; askToFix records that the writer was asked to change something and changes nothing; escalate records that a possible safety concern went to a person and changes nothing; remove takes a published review down (the store's named owner only); erase blanks the writer's data in every version (the store's named owner only). A closed set: there is no other.")
  reason     enum("spam_or_advertising", "profanity", "harassing_or_obscene", "discriminatory", "personal_information", "defamatory", "false_or_dangerous", "believed_fake", "unrelated", "confidential", "undisclosed_connection", "reviewer_request")  @description("Required for decline, askToFix and remove; absent otherwise. The closed set tracks the reasons the FTC's rule on consumer reviews allows a business to withhold a review for, plus spam, profanity and an undisclosed connection; reviewer_request is for a removal only. A rating or a sentiment is never a reason.")
  note       string   @description("Optional note from the person deciding: why, whom a safety concern went to, what the writer was asked to change.")
  revision   int!     @description("The review revision this decision was made on. It covers that revision and no other.")
  contentHash  string  @description("Fingerprint of the words the decision was made on -- headline, text, rating and name. Two edits sent at once can both arrive as one revision; a publish covers only the words it fingerprinted. Empty on a decision recorded before fingerprints, which covers its revision.")
  decidedBy  string!  @description("v1:identity:user.id of the person who decided, read from the caller, never an argument.")
}

@version("1.0.0")
@description("One buyer's review link: a product line of a paid order, at an id derived from (store, order, product) so a line is one link. The link is /reviews/write?product=<handle>&t=<token> on the store's own site; the token is never stored, only its SHA-256. A review written through it is verified. The link closes when its review is published, removed or erased -- read off the review's state, so publishing writes nothing here -- and at expiresAt.")
@displayCard(primary="productHandle", secondary="orderName", tertiary="expiresAt")
@rowAuthz(owner="ownerUserId", clusterOwner, account="accountId")
concept reviewRequest {
  ownerUserId    string!    @description("v1:identity:user.id of the MERCHANT -- the store's site owner, whose borrowed authority the shopper path reads this row under. Stamped by writing as that person.")
  storeId        string!    @description("The store the order was placed on (design D9).")
  accountId      string     @description("The store's organization, copied from the site, so its people read the requests.")
  siteId         string     @description("The v1:platform:site the link points at.")
  orderGid       string!    @description("The mirrored v1:shopify:order this line belongs to.")
  orderName      string     @description("The order's own name, as the store shows it (e.g. #1009).")
  productHandle  string!    @description("The product the link reviews; a review through the link is about this product and no other.")
  productTitle   string     @description("The product's title when the link was made, for the request email.")
  email          string!    @description("The checkout email the request goes to, copied from the order. Personal data: erased with the writer's data on request.")
  tokenHash      string!    @description("SHA-256 (hex) of the link's token. The token itself is never stored, so no read of this row yields a working link.")
  issuedAt       datetime!  @description("When the link was made.")
  expiresAt      datetime!  @description("When the link stops working: issuedAt plus the store's linkLifetimeDays (14 when unset).")
  sentAt         datetime   @description("When the request email went out.")
  sendState      enum("pending", "sent", "skipped", "failed")  @description("Where the request email stands. skipped is a link made by hand, never mailed.")
  sendNote       string     @description("Why it is skipped or failed, in the mail route's own words.")
}

@version("1.2.0")
@description("Runtime reviews settings for one store. The public display toggle lives here as data so a client can hide or show reviews without a deploy or .memql edit.")
@displayCard(primary="publicDisplay", secondary="storeId")
@rowAuthz(owner="ownerUserId", clusterOwner, account="accountId")
concept reviewSettings {
  ownerUserId    string!  @description("v1:identity:user.id of the Client that owns this storefront's review settings.")
  storeId        string!  @description("The store these settings govern (design D9). ONE ROW PER STORE, at the derived id v1:reviews:reviewSettings:<storeId>, because a merchant with a live store and a development store must be able to show reviews on one while they are still hidden on the other -- which is the whole of what previewing a storefront means.")
  publicDisplay  bool!    @description("When true, reviews render on the storefront. Flipped at runtime; not compiled into .memql. The public read consults this FIRST and answers an empty list when it is false, so turning reviews off is one write rather than a deploy.")
  criteriaText   string   @description("Optional client-authored copy describing the closed criteria. Data, not source.")
  accountId      string   @description("The store's organization, so its people read and change these settings.")
  linkLifetimeDays  int   @description("How many days a buyer's review link stays open. Absent means 14.")
  requestDelayDays  int   @description("How many days after an order its review request goes out. Absent means 14.")
  requestsEnabled   bool  @description("Whether this store's review requests go out at all. Absent means off.")
  requestTemplateId string  @description("The v1:campaigns:template.id the review request email is rendered from: the store's own wording.")
  notifyEmail       string  @description("Where 'a review is waiting' goes: one email per review revision, carrying no review text and no writer data.")
  removalApproverUserId string  @description("v1:identity:user.id of the store's owner, the one person who can remove a published review or erase a writer's data. Named by the current owner or the cluster's operators, never by a moderator.")
}
